  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 231 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nLooking ahead to the beginning of next week, Monday will offer a\nslight relief from the heat as temperatures behind the front top\nout in the mid 80s (towards Central MO) to mid 90s (increasing\nfurther south towards the MO/AR border). There's still some\nuncertainty regarding any precipitation chances, as some\nguidance suggests upper level energy pushing through Monday \nmorning/afternoon bringing additional chances (20-40%) for \nshowers towards south-central MO. Additionally, NBM shows a \nlarge spread in temperatures between the 25th and 75th \npercentiles, leading to less confidence in afternoon highs. \nWe'll have to see how the ridging pattern plays out, as that \nwill determine precip chances as well as how the heat builds \nback up.\n\nOnce we get closer to midweek, the upper level ridge will begin\nto push back west of the area, bringing northwesterly flow\naloft. This will lead to more seasonable temperatures in the 80s\nto mid 90s towards the end of the week.",
